      "notes": "All three claims are adequately supported by their quoted evidence at the correct tier. E5 (measurable) reports documented hardship \u2014 the quote is from parliamentary/tax body sources and is accurately represented. E3 (measurable) reports the criticism and retrospective nature \u2014 accurately quoted and not overstated. E28 (measurable) on blanket bans is accurately represented. Tier integrity is sound \u2014 these are historical documented facts, not projections. The mixed direction is genuinely supported: the loan charge element points positive, the IR35 element is genuinely uncertain (review with no committed reform). The biggest_unknown honestly captures the crux. Magnitude (minor) and time_horizon (this-parliament) are reasonable given the narrow affected population and the parliamentary-term framing of a review. No lever leakage, no party identity smuggled in. One minor note: E23 (35% of contractors leaving self-employment) and E22 (120,000 affected) appear in the rationale but are not formally listed as claims with evidence_ids \u2014 this is a pipeline gap but not a blocking issue for this verdict's published claims. The verdict is coherent and defensible."
